[38;5;231m⏺[39m Added to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m:

  - [38;5;153mcreateCheckbox(label, checked)[39m — returns a [38;5;153m<label>[39m containing a native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m and the item text.
    Native input means the on/off state, keyboard toggling, and form semantics come for free.
  - CSS strikethroughs the label via [38;5;153minput:checked + span[39m, so the done state renders without any JS event wiring.
  - One example item is appended to [38;5;153m<main>[39m to show usage; call [38;5;153mcreateCheckbox(...)[39m again for each item you want.

  No tests in the repo, so nothing to run — I checked the page structure only by reading the file.

